@ Chain, chain, join

~ "Apply" Apply
~ "Applicative" append
~ "Arithmetic" mult

.. Apply a quotation that returns a container, and join the results. The quotation is on top.
& Apply f => Chain f
  .. The containers the quotation returns, joined into one.
  chain ( (f a) (a -- (f b)) -- (f b) )

? "chain" < < 1 10 > >
  [ < 1 > [ dup 10 mult swap <> swap append swap append ] chain ]


.. One layer removed. The inner container is the result.
: join ( Chain f => (f (f a)) -- (f a) )
  [] chain

? "join" < < 1 2 3 > > [ < < 1 > < 2 3 > > join ]
? "join empty" < <> > [ < <> <> > join ]

. ..................................................................................................

# Chain Array
  chain = chain_array

: foreign chain_array ( (Array a) (a -- (Array b)) -- (Array b) )
